---
import Head from '../components/Head.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <Head
      title="Privacy notice"
      description="What data news.dehor.com.br actually collects: the newsletter form, local theme preference, and RSS."
      canonicalURL={new URL('/privacy', Astro.site)}
    />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Nav />

    <main>
      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
        <div class="container container--narrow">
          <article class="prose">
            <p>Updated on September 3, 2026</p>
            <h1 id="privacy-title">Privacy notice</h1>
            <p>
              This notice describes the actual data flow of news.dehor.com.br. It should
              receive human and legal review before being treated as a formal policy.
            </p>
            <h2>Newsletter subscription</h2>
            <p>
              The subscription form on the home page and on each project page collects an
              email address and the project(s) you choose to follow. Submissions go to a
              serverless function that forwards them to Resend, the third-party email
              provider used to manage each project's subscriber audience. A hidden field
              exists purely to filter automated spam submissions and is never shown to
              visitors.
            </p>
            <h2>Rate limiting</h2>
            <p>
              To slow down abuse of the subscription form, the server function keeps a
              short-lived, in-memory count of submissions per IP address. This count is not
              written to a database and is not shared with anyone; it exists only in the
              memory of the function while it is running.
            </p>
            <h2>Local preferences and fonts</h2>
            <p>
              The light/dark theme toggle is stored in your browser's local storage and never
              leaves your device. All fonts are self-hosted with the site's own assets, so
              reading this site does not send a request to Google Fonts or any other
              third-party font service. No analytics or tracking script runs on this site.
            </p>
            <h2>RSS and public content</h2>
            <p>
              The RSS feeds and every published edition are public content with no tracking
              attached to reading them.
            </p>
            <h2>Requests</h2>
            <p>
              To request access, correction, or deletion of your subscriber email, contact <a href="mailto:nikolasdehor79@gmail.com">nikolasdehor79@gmail.com</a>. A request may require confirming the email address on file.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
